course: dictionary
lesson: 274
title: Formal words in hospitals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ambulate is a formal word, the kind doctors and nurses use in hospitals and reports. It means to walk or move about. «The patient can ambulate with a frame» tells you the patient can walk, with a frame to help. The context clue is the frame, which is for support while walking.
explain: Ambulate is a verb, so its forms change: ambulates, ambulated, ambulating. «The nurse said the patient ambulated twice today» means the patient walked twice. Most people in everyday life just say «walk», so in ordinary stories that is the better word.
explain: Good writers choose the right word, not the longest one. «He ambulated to the edifice» is a stiff, robot-sounding way to say «He walked to the building». Edifice means building, but it sounds clumsy here. Ask yourself: would a friend say this out loud? If not, pick the simpler word.
fact: Ambulate means to walk or move about.
fact: Ambulate is a formal word, used especially in medical settings.
fact: The verb forms are ambulate, ambulates, ambulated and ambulating.
fact: «The patient can ambulate with a frame» means the patient can walk with a frame to help.
fact: In everyday speech, people usually say «walk» instead of «ambulate».
exercise: «The patient can ambulate with a frame.» What does ambulate mean? | To eat slowly | *To walk or move about | To sleep in a bed | To talk loudly
exercise: In a playground chat, which everyday word means the same as ambulate? | *Walk | Jump | Sing | Swim
exercise: «He ambulated to the edifice.» Which plainer sentence keeps the same meaning? | He shouted at the house | He lay down in the hall | He sang a song | *He walked to the building
test: The nurse says, «Please ambulate to the window.» What does she ask you to do? | *Walk or move about towards the window | Close your eyes | Shout for help | Sit down and rest
test: Which form of ambulate shows something happened in the past? | ambulate | ambulating | ambulates | *ambulated
exam: In «The patient can ambulate with a frame», which everyday word would replace ambulate? | Hide | *Walk | Fly | Sleep
